The instruction "send keys to the VM to open task manager" is typically done via Send Ctrl-Alt-Del. The second point is on "Send Ctrl-Alt-Del", while the first is on "Send Key" (a submenu).

The Ctrl-Alt-Del option is the typical way to open the task manager in Windows. So the second is right.

{"choice": "SECOND"}

In the Qualifier-HSL toolbar, the icons are: picker, picker+, picker-, then feather icons (feather subtract, feather add), then reset. In image 2, the red circle is on the third icon (picker-/something), while feather add (the bold feather with a plus) is at the fifth position, near x=405. In image 3, the red circle is on the icon at x=345, which appears to be the feather add icon (bold feather).

In image 3, the icons are: picker, picker-, picker+, feather-, feather+ (bold, at x=345), reset. The marker sits at x=345 on the bold feather icon, so the second point is the one.

